  "question": {
    "text": "<div>A heat engine operates with the cold reservoir at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>324</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The minimum temperature of the hot reservoir, if the heat engine takes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> heat from the hot reservoir and delivers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> heat to the cold reservoir per cycle, is _____&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>.</div>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "540",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0096_0378a30e2ec0.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 136px;\" /></p><p>Using the relation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Or&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>180</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>324</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>324</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mn>180</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>540</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>"
  }
}